+## STRUCTURE MUST KEEP
+Create one standalone high-angle quarter-view diorama in one cubic virtual space with shared XYZ axes and scale. Use {{one_selected_projection_camera_and_its_line_behavior}} consistently across the base, paving, buildings, walls and exits. Frame the complete square-footprint base and both connected rear boundaries. Extrude the four-corner planar base by consistent depth, with corresponding upper/lower corners on common vertical axes and two visible planar front cuts. No unrequested base curvature, bevels, extra corners, warped walking surface or inconsistent depth. Keep the front open and structural edges/footings readable.
+
+Building ground footprints and player-contact walls follow common X/Y axes: orthogonal masses, L/T/U plans, right-angle setbacks and varied heights are allowed; no rotated buildings, diagonal cuts, wedge gaps or curved building walking boundaries. Connect roof surfaces, ridges/valleys/eaves, wall tops and equipment supports coherently. Tanks, vehicles and props may keep their natural curves/rotation while sharing the camera and grounding.
+
+Keep exactly one functional transition toward back-left (about 11 o'clock) and one toward back-right (about 1 o'clock), as designed below. Preserve the two blocking directions without accidental third routes. Keep the central combat floor and each approach/turn/transition/open-state connection clear as walking volumes with width and height, including clearance for opening mechanisms. Props, rubble and projections stay outside them. Stairs/ramps follow X/Y in plan and connect levels; the front soil cuts are not a third exit. Keep visible blocking structures within the planned approximately 6.5m height bound and preserve full framing.
+
+## CURRENT SCENE
+{{current_place_time_palette_materials_and_active_user_additions_exclusions}}
+{{scene_specific_architecture_masses_boundaries_paving_and_peripheral_props}}
+Left transition: {{within_side_position_form_shown_state_approach_turn_opening_clearance_post_clear_connection_and_entry_role}}.
+Right transition: {{within_side_position_form_shown_state_approach_turn_opening_clearance_post_clear_connection_and_entry_role}}.
+Use these scene-selected positions and forms; neither fixed end gates nor forced alternation is required. Building entrances/internal transitions, alleys, gates, facility passages, stairs and underground ramps are valid. An intentional locked door is distinct from rubble blockage; its approach and future opening route remain usable.
+
+{{per_building_human_entry_roles_and_roof_design_or_no_buildings}}
+Each building has a credible human-scale grounded door/shutter; closed is allowed, actual gameplay entry is optional, and a designated exit may share it without adding another exit. Vents/inspection panels are not entries. Each building roof has 40~80% purposeful equipment/props/functional architecture with credible supports, connections and remaining broad surfaces; shadows, grime, paint and a plain roof do not count. These entry/coverage requirements apply to buildings, not nonbuilding tanks/vehicles/props.
+{{exposed_interior_depth_entry_aisle_functional_space_and_cutaway_visibility_or_not_applicable}}
+{{place_specific_front_ground_layers_foundations_and_large_functional_infrastructure}}
+{{place_wide_age_repair_and_recovered_technology_relationships}}
+{{new_scene_design_distinctions_or_explicit_edit_target_preservation_and_own_correction}}
+
+## ART / REFERENCE ROLES
+Use Little Devil Inside architectural form/material/light/color expression with large readable forms, broad organized color fields, selective substantial wear and restrained detail. Retain old repaired surfaces; avoid uniform micro-scratches/rust/gravel, blur, all-plastic materials, extreme low-poly or photoreal miniature density. Distinguish metal, wood, cloth, glass and water through broad material cues and restrained reflections. Keep thickness, grounding and mechanical joins readable. Use {{scene_lighting_and_atmosphere}} without hiding base/footing/paving lines, roofs, exits, center or cuts. No unrequested people/monsters, text/numbers/slogans/arrows/UI; use only limited necessary signage.
+
+The world is Salvage Cyberpunk: recovered advanced technology with visible repair, replacement and current function across the place, translated into this restrained 3D expression. Maintain a readable mechanical presence relative to architecture without a fixed global ratio, indiscriminate mechanization or copied devices.
+
+{{actual_input_indices_and_roles_geometry_guide_M01_M02_art_M03_world_M04_edit_target_if_any}}
+Structure inputs govern projection, base and connectivity; their original buildings, gate coordinates, pipe patterns, neon theme and diagram labels are not fixed scene designs. Art/world inputs supply only their assigned expression/design roles; exclude their camera and layout. Do not import the LDI world/story/characters/UI or M04 characters/photoreal surface density. {{selected_supplement_specific_exclusions_including_M03_12_building_only_when_used_and_scoped_example_limits}}
